One country worth knowing that isn't on the list: **Vietnam** is the world's second-largest coffee producer, but it grows mostly robusta, so you'll find it in instant coffee and blends more than on a specialty shelf.

## Where to start

If you've mostly had coffee from the grocery store, a washed coffee from **Colombia** or **Guatemala** will taste familiar, just better. A light roast from **Ethiopia** or **Kenya** is the quickest way to find out why people get so excited about origin. And if you like a heavy, earthy cup with milk, try **Sumatra**.

Next up is [variety](/coffee/guides/coffee-varieties/): the kind of coffee plant the beans came from.
